hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"371","'Isa ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Damrah, from Sa'd ibn 'Abdullah ibn Sa'd, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whatever shepherd seeks profit at the expense of his flock, his flock is ruined."
"372","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Muhammad — meaning Ibn Ja'far — narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Mughirah: I heard al-Sha'bi (say), that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to take the pledge from the women, a Qatari cloak was brought and he placed it upon his hand, then said: ""I do not shake hands with women."
